      "bibliographic_citation": "Tacza, J., & Bozoki, T., Raita, T. (2026). The first-mode Schumann resonance frequency response to threshold-defined HSS/CIR proxy onsets (Version 1). University of Oulu, Sodankyl\u00e4 Geophysical Observatory",
      "cumulative_state": 0,
      "data_catalog": "urn:nbn:fi:att:data-catalog-ida",
      "description": {
        "en": "This data set is processed from the time series of the first-mode Schumann resonance frequency observed by the Finnish Pulsation Magnetometer Network (FinPuMa) based on the analysis by Bozoki et al. (https://doi.org/10.3389/feart.2021.689127). The data set intentionally contains event-window processed data, not the full continuous Schumann resonance archive.\n\nProcessed event-window data is collected for  a manuscript \"Schumann Resonance Frequency Increase Following Recurrent Solar Wind Stream Onsets\" by Jos\u00e9 C. Tacza, Gabriella S\u00e1tori, Anne Neska, Tero Raita, Tamas Bozoki\"  on the first-mode Schumann resonance frequency response to threshold-defined HSS/CIR proxy onsets accepted to Earth and Space Science (ESS) journal.\n\n Data set contains processed daily data around the 173 threshold-defined proxy onsets used in the manuscript. It is designed to let readers inspect the event list, station-specific valid-event support, event-window Schumann resonance measurements, ICME-overlap flags used for the main figures and Table S1 in the manuscript.\n\nEvent definition:\nCandidate onsets were identified from a 3-day moving median of solar-wind speed, where `Vsw >= 500 km/s` and the increase relative to two days earlier was at least `80 km/s`, with a minimum 20-day separation between accepted onsets.\n\nThese events are described as threshold-defined HSS/CIR proxy onsets, not as a formal external HSS/CIR catalog.\n\nTime windows:\nAll event-window tables use:\n- event window: days -15 to +20 relative to onset\n- baseline window: days  -15 to -5 relative to onset\n- response window: days  0 to +1 relative to onset\n\nThe daily time stamp is represented as a UTC date. The response values used in the manuscript are baseline-subtracted values, stored as `delta_from_baseline`.\n\nValidity flags:\n\nThe event-window SR tables preserve all 173 onsets and provide inclusion flags:\n- `included_in_final_station_composite`: event/station/component satisfies the manuscript baseline and response validity rules.\n- `included_in_matched_support_106`: event is valid for weighted-average AVG F1 at HRN, IVA, and ROV.\n- `included_in_final_hrn_lorentz_composite`: HRN Lorentz-fit event/component/variable satisfies the Figure 1 validity rules.\n\nThe validity rule is at least 6 finite baseline days in days `-15` to `-5` and at least one finite response value in days `0` to `+1`.\n\nJos\u00e9 Tacza acknowledges funding from the National Science Centre, Poland (Grant 2023/51/D/ST10/01757)."
      },
